    "decision_rationale": "Although K=3 achieves a higher mathematical silhouette score (0.4412 vs 0.4065), it causes severe commercial over-aggregation: it collapses Champions (INR 113k spend, 25 orders) and Steady Repeaters (INR 39k spend, 8.6 orders) into a single 45.5% cluster, and lumps hot Recent Low-Ticket trial buyers (recency 14.8 days) with cold Lapsed customers (recency 274.8 days) into a single 47.6% cluster. K=5 cuts within-cluster error (inertia) by 46.0% (from 6,544.5 to 3,534.7) and provides five distinct, actionable customer personas necessary for retention marketing."
  },
